# Review package: batch 4, slice node

## 767f2701 Number the node messages that change data, in the protocol

A node will keep each message that changes the company's data until the server confirms it, so the protocol gains the
numbers and the confirmation. NUMBERED lists the messages a node numbers, each gains an optional n (an integer from 1),
hello gains an optional stream (a uuid), and a server message ack { upto } confirms every number up to upto. ACKS_HEADER
names the header a server sends on its upgrade answer to say it confirms. Every addition is optional or a message an
older side drops, so builds one version apart still talk.

The node's main.ts ignores ack for now so the node still compiles; the outbox commit that follows handles it.

Ruling: job.program, agent.hook_rejected and agent.unheard are in NUMBERED, agent.restarted and node.stopping are not - why: map ruling 5, taken by the lead - cost if wrong: a message numbered by mistake waits in the outbox, a message left out is lost in a restart.
Ruling: the server part of Task 4 (hub, messages, socket, app, FakeNode) is not in this commit - why: the brief gives only the protocol part to this lane - cost if wrong: none here, the server lane lands it after.
Ruling: main.ts of the node drops ack in this commit - why: the new server message must compile in the node's switch - cost if wrong: none, the next commit replaces the line.

